# A synthetic TrueType font — glyph 1 a simple glyph of two contours, 14 points; glyph 2 a
# COMPOSITE of two glyph-1 components; glyph 3 a composite of glyph 1 then glyph 2 (nested);
# glyph 0 empty; on 2 variants a glyph 4 with an outline and a program of its own; a 16-entry
# cvt, a two-function fpgm — in 39 VARIANTS that differ from font 0 (prep RTG) in their prep,
# their fpgm, one maxp field, their composite records, an hmtx entry, hhea.descender, a vmtx
# or a glyph 4 (each says which below), and 167 glyph PROGRAMS run through FreeType itself at
# their ppem on their font. For each program: the bytes, the glyph FreeType loaded, and what
# its glyph slot held afterwards — every outline point's hinted position (F26Dot6), its tag
# byte, and the advance. Every program was ALSO loaded under FT_LOAD_PEDANTIC on a fresh face
# and loaded clean, so no instruction was skipped silently. And for EVERY row, glyphs 1, 2 and
# 3 of its font were loaded in that order on ONE face at the row's ppem — the consumer's
# flow, `prep` once — and glyph 2's and 3's outlines recorded (hu_expect2_*, hu_expect3_*),
