fn hu_ft_version(): i64 { return "2.14.3"; }

# The fonts: sfnt tables cmap cvt fpgm glyf head hhea hmtx loca maxp post prep (plus vhea + vmtx on `c_vmtx`).
# maxp of font 0: 14 points, 2 contours, 42 composite points, 6 composite contours, 2 zones,
# 16 twilight points, 32 storage, 64 functions, 4 IDEFs, 128 stack elements, 159 bytes of
# instructions, 2 component elements, depth 2. cvt entry i is i * 101 - 505
# (programs/hint_test.cyr's). fpgm of font 0 defines function 3 (adds 5) and 7 (adds 1):
#   PUSHB 3 FDEF PUSHB 5 ADD ENDF PUSHB 7 FDEF PUSHB 1 ADD ENDF
# Glyph 2 of font 0: [0x0007 gid 1 (0, 0)] [0x0007 gid 1 (600, 0)] with instructions.
# Glyph 3 of font 0: [0x0007 gid 1 (0, 0)] [0x0007 gid 2 (0, 500)] with instructions.
# hmtx of font 0: glyph 0 advance 600 lsb 0, glyph 1 advance 600 lsb 98, glyph 2 advance 1200 lsb 98, glyph 3
#   advance 1200 lsb 98.
# Glyphs 1, 2 and 3 carry no program in these copies (a composite keeps its WE_HAVE_INSTR flag
# with n_ins 0 where its variant sets it); a glyph 4 carries its own. Each font's prep
# (`prep:`), and, where a font differs from font 0 in more than its prep, which tables
# (`differs:`) and the fpgm listing:
#   font 0 `rtg`, 844 bytes: the default round state restated; every program not about a table runs under it
#     prep: RTG
#   font 1 `gs_carry`, 852 bytes: four of the graphics-state fields FreeType keeps from a prep for every glyph
#   program
#     prep: PUSHB 96 SMD PUSHB 40 SCVTCI PUSHB 10 SDB PUSHB 4 SDS
#   font 2 `wcvtf`, 848 bytes: cvt 8 becomes 400 font units (300 at 12 ppem) for the size
#     prep: PUSHB 8 PUSHW 400 WCVTF
#   font 3 `deltac`, 848 bytes: cvt 8 gains 8 steps of 1/8 px at 12 ppem (band 3 of base 9) and nothing at 28
#     prep: PUSHB 63 8 1 DELTAC1
#   font 4 `idef_91`, 848 bytes: prep defines opcode 0x91 (GETVARIATION on a variation face) as SHPIX 64: on a
#   static face FreeType runs the IDEF (ref2143/ttinterp.c:7306-7314; LaoUI.ttf does this)
#     prep: RTG PUSHB 145 IDEF PUSHB 64 SHPIX ENDF
#   font 5 `idef_four`, 872 bytes: prep defines the unassigned opcodes 0x28, 0x7B, 0x8F and 0xA0 (all four
#   maxInstructionDefs slots) as SHPIX by 64, 32, 16 and 8
#     prep: RTG PUSHB 40 IDEF PUSHB 64 SHPIX ENDF PUSHB 123 IDEF PUSHB 32 SHPIX ENDF PUSHB 143 IDEF PUSHB 16
#   SHPIX ENDF PUSHB 160 IDEF PUSHB 8 SHPIX ENDF
#   font 6 `idef_std`, 848 bytes: prep IDEFs 0x60 (ADD): a standard instruction is dispatched before the IDEF
#   table is looked at, so the definition is never reached
#     prep: RTG PUSHB 96 IDEF PUSHB 64 SHPIX ENDF
#   font 7 `fdef_sparse`, 852 bytes: fpgm REPLACED: functions 0 (SHPIX 32), 1 (SHPIX 16) and 100 (SHPIX 64)
#   with maxp.maxFunctionDefs 3 — FreeType bounds the COUNT of definitions, not the numbers
#   (ref2143/ttinterp.c:3283-3309)
#     prep: RTG
#     differs: fpgm; maxp.maxFunctionDefs 3
#     fpgm: PUSHB 0 FDEF PUSHB 32 SHPIX ENDF PUSHB 1 FDEF PUSHB 16 SHPIX ENDF PUSHB 100 FDEF PUSHB 64 SHPIX
#   ENDF
#   font 8 `fpgm_getinfo`, 872 bytes: fpgm EXTENDED: function 9 is defined under IF on GETINFO's grayscale bit
#   AT FPGM TIME (SHPIX 128 when set, 64 when clear) and function 10 answers GETINFO 32 when called
#     prep: RTG
#     differs: fpgm
#     fpgm: PUSHB 3 FDEF PUSHB 5 ADD ENDF PUSHB 7 FDEF PUSHB 1 ADD ENDF PUSHB 32 GETINFO IF PUSHB 9 FDEF PUSHB
#   128 SHPIX ENDF ELSE PUSHB 9 FDEF PUSHB 64 SHPIX ENDF EIF PUSHB 10 FDEF PUSHB 32 GETINFO ENDF
#   font 9 `fdef_floor`, 844 bytes: fpgm REPLACED: functions 5 (SHPIX 64) and 9 (SHPIX 32) with
#   maxp.maxFunctionDefs 1 — FreeType's maxp loader floors maxFunctionDefs at 64 (measured on 2.14.3: 64
#   definitions load under a declared 1, 65 fail), so two definitions fit
#     prep: RTG
#     differs: fpgm; maxp.maxFunctionDefs 1
#     fpgm: PUSHB 5 FDEF PUSHB 64 SHPIX ENDF PUSHB 9 FDEF PUSHB 32 SHPIX ENDF
#   font 10 `c_round`, 844 bytes: glyph 2's second component at offset (0, -128) WITH ROUND_XY_TO_GRID: at 12
#   ppem the scaled offset -96 is an exact negative half, FT_PIX_ROUND's floor form gives -64
