# The consumer-flow records (hu_expect2_* / hu_expect3_*): row p's hu_x<p>(k) chunks hold one
# space-separated decimal text — glyph 2's record then glyph 3's, each `points contours advance
# end.. x y tag..` (a glyph not recorded is the single number -1) — and hu_num(p, k) reads the
# k-th number of it, counting across the chunks (a chunk boundary separates two numbers).
